# Personal / machine-specific - never commit (mod paths, transfer log, undo backups)
config/
HANDOFF.md
# Split out of HANDOFF.md on 2026-09-13. The stage-by-stage history is internal
# notes and stays local. RELEASE.md came OUT of this list on 2026-09-20, for
# the reason the old comment here anticipated: there is a second person on the
# repo now, CLAUDE.md points every session at RELEASE.md as the only prose copy
# of the release rules, and a clone did not contain it.
HANDOFF_ARCHIVE.md
med2_mod_installer.iss

# Generated / regenerable
.cache/
dist/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/

# Captured suite output. A full run redirected to a file, kept while somebody
# reads it and regenerable by running the suite again - never a source of truth
# about what passes. The suite prints its own tally; that is the answer.
main/results.txt
main/test_results.txt

# A path that was meant to be a path and became a filename. Writing to
# `C:\temp\foo.txt` from the POSIX shell here does not resolve as a Windows
# path, so the whole string lands as ONE file in main/ - with the colon stored
# as U+F03A, because Windows will not take a real one. Four of these sat in
# main/ from 2026-09-14 to 2026-09-20.
# THIS LINE IS A NET, NOT THE FIX: if one appears, the thing to correct is the
# command that wrote it (use the scratchpad directory), not this file.
main/C?temp*

# Local tool config, not part of the project. CLAUDE.md came OUT of this list
# on 2026-09-20: it is the project's own instructions - which documents to read,
# how the two release lines work, which agent to hand what - and with a second
# contributor on the repo it has to travel with a clone. `.claude/` stays local
# because the agents and settings in it are this machine's.
.claude/
graphify-out/
.gitattributes

# Saved reference material - TWC tutorial pages with their whole _files asset
# dumps, the ModdingTool source, the Sounds Parser and Sprite prototypes. 3.4 GB
# of other people's work, kept locally to read; none of it ours to redistribute.
# The generated INDEX is the exception: it is ours, it is small, and it is what
# every later phase greps to find the tutorial for a format. A parent directory
# that is excluded can't have its children re-included, so the exclusion is
# spelled out level by level to leave a hole for it.
main/Reference/*
!main/Reference/TWCenter/
main/Reference/TWCenter/*
!main/Reference/TWCenter/INDEX.md
!main/Reference/TWCenter/INDEX.json

# Third-party reference tools kept locally for comparison (not ours to ship)
UnitEditor11/
# Saved TWC tutorial pages + Gigantus' sprite setup, kept for reference. The only
# part the tool actually needs (nvcompress + its DLLs) is vendored in
# main/vendor/nvtt/.
Sprite/

# Superseded work kept around locally (old builds, the Sounds Parser prototype)
Old Files/

# Raw unpacked vanilla UI: ~300 MB of TGA straight out of the .pack files, over
# half of it the same picture under several names.
# `main/dev/release/pack_vanilla_ui.py` turns it into main/vanilla_ui/ -
# deduplicated lossless WebP, ~6x smaller - and THAT
# is what gets committed. This stays local.
unpackaded_vanilla_ui/
unpackaded_vanilla_ui.7z

# Runtime logs (server.log.sample IS committed as a reference; real logs are not)
server.log
launcher-output.txt
troubleshoot-output.txt

# Editor/OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# dev/checks/run_suites.py writes its report here
main/dev/checks/suite_report.*
